{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An unmeasured tremolo."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTremolo","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTremolo\/Kind-swift.enum"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTremolo\/Kind-swift.enum\/unmeasured"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"unmeasured"}],"symbolKind":"case","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLTremoloV4KindO10unmeasuredyA2EmF","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Case","title":"MXLTremolo.Kind.unmeasured"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltremolo\/kind-swift.enum\/unmeasured"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"unmeasured"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTremolo/Kind-swift.enum/unmeasured":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"An unmeasured tremolo.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLTremolo.Kind.unmeasured","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTremolo\/Kind-swift.enum\/unmeasured","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltremolo\/kind-swift.enum\/unmeasured","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"unmeasured","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTremolo":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTremolo"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTremolo","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTremolo"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltremolo","title":"MXLTremolo","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tremolo ornament can be used to indicate single-note, double-note, or unmeasured tremolos. Single-note"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tremolos use the single type, double-note tremolos use the start and stop types, and unmeasured tremolos use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the unmeasured type. The default is “single” for compatibility with Version 1.1. The text of the element"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indicates the number of tremolo marks and is an integer from 0 to 8. Note that the number of attached beams is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not included in this value, but is represented separately using the beam element. The value should be 0 for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unmeasured tremolos."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTremolo/Kind-swift.enum":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The tremolo-type is used to distinguish double-note, single-note, and unmeasured tremolos.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLTremolo.Kind","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTremolo\/Kind-swift.enum","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltremolo\/kind-swift.enum","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Kind","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Kind","kind":"identifier"}]}}}